Title: The Ember Crown
Credit: Written by
Author: Previz Stage
Draft date: 2026-10-24

EXT. ANCIENT FOREST CLEARING - DAWN

Mist hangs between colossal moss-covered trunks. Shafts of pale gold light cut through the canopy onto a ring of standing stones. Fireflies drift above the ferns.

WREN (20s, slight, wild copper hair under a hooded green cloak, a longbow across her back) kneels at the edge of the stones, reading tracks in the dew.

A dragon, dark against the dawn sky, circles slowly far overhead.

BRANNOCK (50s, broad, grey-bearded, dented iron breastplate over a leather jerkin, a two-handed sword on his hip) steps out of the mist behind her.

BRANNOCK
You should not be out past the wards alone.

WREN
(not looking up)
The wards fell at midnight. Something walked through them.

BRANNOCK
Then we leave. Now.

WREN
It left the crown. Right there, in the stones.

INT. THRONE HALL OF KARRACK - NIGHT

A vast stone hall lit by torches in iron brackets and a fire pit the size of a cart. Faded banners hang from the rafters. A cracked obsidian throne stands on a dais at the far end.

Wren stands before the dais, the crown wrapped in cloth. Brannock waits a step behind her, hand on his sword.

BRANNOCK
Say it plainly. Who sent you?

WREN
No one sent me. The forest did.

BRANNOCK
The forest does not give orders.

WREN
(setting the crown on the dais)
It did tonight.
